
node_modules/
*.log
out/

# tsc -b incremental state. Rewritten by every build and tracked until now, so
# it turned up dirty in every diff and every commit -- derived state competing
# with source for review attention. Deleting it only costs one non-incremental
# rebuild.
*.tsbuildinfo

packages/
docs/_build/

# NOTHING GENERATED IS IGNORED HERE ANY MORE, and the absence is the point.
#
# server/src/generated/ held an ANTLR lexer and parser generated from
# src/PSS*.g4. There is no ANTLR front end in this repository now: the server
# parses through @psstools/pssparser, the pssparser C++ core compiled to
# WebAssembly, which ivpm fetches and npm's `prepare` hook builds. The grammar
# is upstream's, and so is the generation of it.
#
# server/src/core/ast/generated/ is likewise not ignored, but for the opposite
# reason -- it is a checked-in re-export of the AST classes that ship inside
# @psstools/pssparser, so that the parser and this server share one set of
# constructors. See the header in that file; `instanceof` depends on it.
#
# packages/ above is where ivpm puts the parser, and covers the built wasm.

.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/

